Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add integration and UI test projects for the course
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The three-day course teaches the test pyramid, so the repository needs a level
for each. It had only unit tests, and they referenced Rpn.Core alone.

  · Rpn.IntegrationTests hosts the real app through WebApplicationFactory
    against an in-memory SQLite database
  · Rpn.UiTests drives a browser with Playwright, in MSTest because Playwright
    ships no xUnit base class
  · Program is now a public partial class so the factory can name it
  · two accounts are seeded in development, so an exercise needing a second
    signed-in user does not start with twenty manual registrations

None of the nine planted defects is touched. Both new projects carry only
smoke tests: what they are for is written during the labs.

Not compiled. No .NET SDK was reachable from the environment that wrote this.
